1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,950
Hunter?

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:05,950
Grant. Hey. Hunter, from Ops. We met
at, uh… onboarding.

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:07,950
Right. Ops.

4
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:11,950
Swing by twenty-two later. Let's talk
about your… department.

5
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:14,093
Twenty-two?! What did you do?

6
00:00:14,143 --> 00:00:14,950
Spreadsheet thing.

7
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:18,950
Nobody gets called to twenty-two for a
spreadsheet.

8
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:27,950
Phone. In. It's an hour.

9
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:31,950
Everything'll still be on fire when
you get out.

10
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:51,233
Can I tell you something weird? When I
was like nineteen I told myself I'd

11
00:00:51,283 --> 00:00:53,950
relax once I, you know, made it.

12
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:54,450
And?

13
00:00:54,500 --> 00:00:57,950
I never decided what 'made it' was.

14
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:01,950
Okay. What would it be? If you had to
pick.

15
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:03,950
…This is pretty close.

16
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:06,950
This was eighty-nine bucks. For two.

17
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:08,950
Then I'm a cheap date.

18
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:13,950
Can I say something kind of petty?

19
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:17,950
My dad was always about to be rich.
Big plans.

20
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:20,950
He promised my abuela Lisbon. Never
happened.

21
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:25,950
So when people flash money… I kind of
stop trusting them.

22
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:28,450
Anyway. You're not like that.

23
00:01:28,500 --> 00:01:28,950
…No.

24
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:36,950
…Board vote?
